      "lineAnnotations": {
        "9294": {"synopsis":"Calls ROM 0's $3FF0 with A = 0 and the zero flag set, HL as given, and returns what it\nreturns. Unlike v4.1's routine it keeps nothing: CURCHL, FLAGS and FLAGS2 are not saved\nround the call. ROM 1 hands this routine's address to this ROM in HL (ROM 1 $242C, before\nits call of DOS_JUMPS $014E), so it is called back from there rather than from this ROM's\nown code.\nEntry: HL = the value ROM 0's routine takes.\nExit: as ROM 0's $3FF0 returns.","comment":"A = 0, zero flag set"},
        "9295": {"comment":"Call ROM 0's $3FF0"},
        "9298": {"synopsis":"CALL_ROM0's address: $3FF0 in ROM 0."},
        "9300": {"comment":"Back with ROM 0's result"},
        "9301": {"synopsis":"As ROM0_HOOK_A0, but A is passed on as it is (the zero flag set if A is 0, carry clear). ROM\n1 hands this address over in HL at ROM 1 $2487, before its call of DOS_JUMPS $0154.\nEntry: A, HL = the values ROM 0's $3FF0 takes.\nExit: as ROM 0's $3FF0 returns.","comment":"A kept, zero flag set if A is 0"},
        "9302": {"comment":"Call ROM 0's $3FF0"},
        "9305": {"synopsis":"CALL_ROM0's address: $3FF0 in ROM 0."},
        "9307": {"comment":"Back with ROM 0's result"},
        "9308": {"synopsis":"The disk drive test program, $245C-$305B of this ROM copied to $6000-$6BFF and run there\nwith ROM 1 and RAM bank 0 paged in (ROM 0 $356D copies $0C00 bytes and ROM 0 $358E calls\n$6000). Every address the code uses (calls, jumps, messages, variables) is its RAM address,\n$3BA4 above the ROM address; relative jumps read the same in both. The ROM 1 RST $28 calls\nthe ROM 3 address in the word after it. This entry ($6000) clears the screen, opens stream\n2, runs the test (DT_RUN) and prints \"The disk drive test passed.\" or, after the disk error\nmessage when A is not $FF, \"The disk drive test failed.\". It then asks for R to run it all\nagain or Q to return.\nExit: AF = the test's result (carry set if it passed; otherwise A = a disk error number, or\n$FF when the failure was already reported).","comment":"ROM 1 and RAM bank 0 in"},
        "9311": {"comment":"Clear the screen (ROM 3's $0D6B)"},
        "9314": {"comment":"Open stream 2, the main screen (ROM 3's $1601)"},
        "9319": {"comment":"Run the test: carry set if every drive passed"},
        "9322": {"comment":"Keep its result"},
        "9323": {"comment":"HL = \"The disk drive test passed.\""},
        "9326": {"comment":"Passed?"},
        "9328": {"comment":"A not $FF: print disk error A first"},
        "9333": {"comment":"HL = \"The disk drive test failed.\""},
        "9336": {"synopsis":"Prints the verdict and asks for R or Q.","comment":"Print the verdict"},
        "9339": {"comment":"\"Press R to repeat, Q to quit\""},
        "9344": {"comment":"HL = the test's AF"},
        "9345": {"synopsis":"Waits for R or Q, upper or lower case."},
        "9346": {"comment":"Wait for a key"},
        "9350": {"comment":"Upper case"},
        "9352": {"comment":"R: run it all again"},
        "9357": {"comment":"Not Q: wait for another key"},
        "9361": {"comment":"AF = the test's result"},
        "9364": {"synopsis":"Runs the test on every drive found: prints the title, calls DOS_JUMPS $0100, and checks with\nDOS_JUMPS $0157 that the controller answers (\"NO DISK INTERFACE !\" otherwise). DOS_JUMPS\n$017B says whether drive B is there; the drives found are printed (\"Found Drive(s) :A\" or\n\":A&B\") and the last one's letter kept at $6AA3. After DOS_JUMPS $0178 with A = 0 and IX =\n$6A61 it tests drive A (DT_TEST_DRIVE) and then drive B if there is one.\nExit: carry set if every drive passed; carry clear with A = $FF after a failure already\nreported, or with A = the error a DOS call returned.","comment":"Print the title"},
        "9369": {"comment":"ROM 2 and RAM bank 7 in"},
        "9372": {"comment":"DOS_JUMPS $0100"},
        "9375": {"comment":"Failed: return its error"},
        "9378": {"comment":"Failed?"},
        "9379": {"comment":"ROM 2 and RAM bank 7 in"},
        "9382": {"comment":"DOS_JUMPS $0157: carry set if the controller answers"},
        "9385": {"comment":"ROM 1 and RAM bank 0 back in"},
        "9388": {"comment":"Controller there?"},
        "9390": {"comment":"\"NO DISK INTERFACE !\" and \"Test Aborted.\""},
        "9395": {"comment":"Carry clear and A = $FF: already reported"},
        "9399": {"synopsis":"The controller answered: list the drives.","comment":"Drive 0 (A) is tested first"},
        "9403": {"comment":"\"Found Drive(s) :A\""},
        "9408": {"comment":"ROM 2 and RAM bank 7 in"},
        "9411": {"comment":"DOS_JUMPS $017B: carry set if drive 1 answers"},
        "9414": {"comment":"ROM 1 and RAM bank 0 back in"},
        "9417": {"comment":"Only drive A: the last drive is 'A'"},
        "9421": {"comment":"Print \"&B\""},
        "9427": {"comment":"The last drive is 'B'"},
        "9429": {"synopsis":"Notes the last drive's letter and starts the tests.","comment":"Note the last drive's letter"},
        "9432": {"comment":"End the line"},
        "9435": {"comment":"IX = the parameter block at $6A61"},
        "9439": {"comment":"A = 0 for it"},
        "9441": {"comment":"ROM 2 and RAM bank 7 in"},
        "9444": {"comment":"DOS_JUMPS $0178"},
        "9447": {"comment":"ROM 1 and RAM bank 0 back in"},
        "9450": {"comment":"Failed?"},
        "9451": {"comment":"Test drive A"},
        "9454": {"comment":"Failed?"},
        "9455": {"comment":"Then drive 1 (B)"},
        "9460": {"comment":"Is there a drive B?"},
        "9465": {"comment":"Test it too"},
        "9469": {"synopsis":"Tests the drive whose number is at $6AA4 with the two sides of a test disk.\n1. \"Testing Drive \" and the drive's letter; if a disk is in, asks for it to be removed and\n   waits until the drive is not ready, then asks for side 1 and waits until it is ready.\n2. After DOS_JUMPS $015A: formats track 0 with the filler at $6860 (DT_FORMAT_TRACK) and\n   measures the drive's speed (DT_SPIN_TEST), giving up if it is 3 % or more out; then\n   DOS_JUMPS $015A again.\n3. Formats tracks 19, 0 and 39 filled with $E5 and tracks 18, 1 and 38 with $AA, and reads\n   them back (DT_READ_CHECK); then formats tracks 0, 1, 18, 19, 38 and 39 with $00 and reads\n   those back.\n4. Asks for the disk out, clears the screen, asks for side 2 and waits for it. That side\n   must be write protected (\"Disk is not write-protected.\" otherwise): its tracks 39 to 0\n   are read and each must hold $11 times (track + 1) in every byte.\n5. Asks for the disk out and clears the screen.\nExit: carry set and A = 0 if the drive passed; carry clear with A = $FF after a failure\nalready reported (the spin test included), or with A = the error a DOS call returned.","comment":"\"Testing Drive \""},
        "9474": {"comment":"The drive's letter"},
        "9480": {"comment":"End the line"},
        "9483": {"comment":"Disk in the drive already?"},
        "9488": {"comment":"\"Remove disk from drive\""},
        "9493": {"synopsis":"Waits until the drive is not ready.","comment":"Wait until the drive is not ready"},
        "9498": {"synopsis":"Asks for side 1 of the test disk.","comment":"\"Insert side 1 of test disk.\""},
        "9503": {"synopsis":"Waits until the drive is ready.","comment":"Wait until the drive is ready"},
        "9508": {"comment":"ROM 2 and RAM bank 7 in"},
        "9511": {"comment":"DOS_JUMPS $015A"},
        "9514": {"comment":"ROM 1 and RAM bank 0 back in"},
        "9517": {"comment":"Track 0 first, with the filler at $6860"},
        "9519": {"comment":"Format it (DT_FORMAT_TRACK)"},
        "9522": {"comment":"Failed?"},
        "9523": {"comment":"Measure the drive's speed (DT_SPIN_TEST)"},
        "9526": {"comment":"3 % or more out?"},
        "9527": {"comment":"ROM 2 and RAM bank 7 in"},
        "9530": {"comment":"DOS_JUMPS $015A again"},
        "9533": {"comment":"ROM 1 and RAM bank 0 back in"},
        "9536": {"comment":"\"Formatting tracks.\""},
        "9541": {"comment":"Filler $E5 for tracks 19, 0 and 39"},
        "9546": {"comment":"Track 19"},
        "9551": {"comment":"Failed?"},
        "9552": {"comment":"Track 0"},
        "9557": {"comment":"Failed?"},
        "9558": {"comment":"Track 39"},
