        "9703": {"comment":"Track 39"},
        "9708": {"comment":"Failed?"},
        "9709": {"comment":"\"Remove disk from drive\""},
        "9714": {"synopsis":"Waits until the drive is not ready.","comment":"Wait until the drive is not ready"},
        "9719": {"comment":"Clear the whole screen (ROM 3's $0DAF)"},
        "9722": {"comment":"\"Insert side 2 of test disk.\""},
        "9727": {"synopsis":"Waits until the drive is ready.","comment":"Wait until the drive is ready"},
        "9732": {"comment":"ROM 2 and RAM bank 7 in"},
        "9735": {"comment":"DOS_JUMPS $015A"},
        "9738": {"comment":"ROM 1 and RAM bank 0 back in"},
        "9741": {"comment":"C = the drive"},
        "9745": {"comment":"ROM 2 and RAM bank 7 in"},
        "9748": {"comment":"DOS_JUMPS $017E: A = the drive's status"},
        "9751": {"comment":"ROM 1 and RAM bank 0 back in"},
        "9754": {"comment":"Write protected (bit 6)?"},
        "9758": {"comment":"\"Disk is not write-protected.\""},
        "9763": {"comment":"Carry clear and A = $FF: already reported"},
        "9767": {"synopsis":"Side 2 is write protected: checks its data.","comment":"\"Checking Data.\""},
        "9772": {"comment":"Tracks 39 down to 0"},
        "9774": {"synopsis":"One track of side 2 (DT_CHECK_SIDE2).","comment":"Keep the count"},
        "9775": {"comment":"Expected byte: $11 times (track + 1)"},
        "9784": {"comment":"D = the track"},
        "9786": {"comment":"Every byte as expected?"},
        "9790": {"comment":"Failed?"},
        "9791": {"comment":"Next track down"},
        "9793": {"comment":"\"Remove disk from drive\""},
        "9798": {"synopsis":"Waits until the drive is not ready.","comment":"Wait until the drive is not ready"},
        "9803": {"comment":"Clear the whole screen (ROM 3's $0DAF)"},
        "9806": {"comment":"A = 0 and carry set: the drive passed"},
        "9809": {"synopsis":"Measures the drive's speed; DT_TEST_DRIVE calls it after formatting track 0 of side 1 (the\nmessage \"Spin test not implemented.\" is in the table but not used). It times the 765's READ\nDATA for a sector $FE twice (DT_TIME_TURN) and compares the second count with $4C2D, putting\n'+' (below) or '-' (at or above) into the message \"Spin speed difference *00 %\" at $6521.\nThe difference is divided by $00C3 counts a per cent, 99 if the count reaches $10000, and\nadded to the message's \"00\"; \"Spin speed is INCORRECT !\" follows at 3 % or more.\nExit: A = $FF; carry set if the difference is under 3 %.","comment":"\"Starting spin-speed test.\""},
        "9814": {"comment":"Time a READ DATA once (its count is dropped)"},
        "9817": {"comment":"And again: DE:HL = the count"},
        "9820": {"comment":"The figure starts as \"00\""},
        "9828": {"comment":"Keep the count's high word"},
        "9829": {"comment":"Keep the low word"},
        "9832": {"comment":"Above or below $4C2D?"},
        "9838": {"comment":"'-' when at or above it"},
        "9842": {"comment":"'+' when below"},
        "9844": {"synopsis":"Puts the sign into the message.","comment":"Into the message"},
        "9847": {"comment":"A = the high word, the comparison's carry kept"},
        "9850": {"comment":"High word 0?"},
        "9854": {"comment":"Too far out: report 99 %"},
        "9859": {"synopsis":"The count is under $10000: work out the difference.","comment":"Carry from the comparison"},
        "9860": {"comment":"HL = the count"},
        "9866": {"comment":"Below $4C2D: subtract the other way"},
        "9869": {"synopsis":"HL = the difference from $4C2D, A = 0.","comment":"A = 0, the per cent count"},
        "9870": {"comment":"HL = the difference"},
        "9872": {"comment":"One per cent is $00C3 counts"},
        "9875": {"synopsis":"Counts whole $00C3s in the difference.","comment":"Another $00C3 in it?"},
        "9880": {"comment":"One per cent more"},
        "9883": {"synopsis":"Puts the per cent figure A into the message and prints it.","comment":"Keep the per cent figure"},
        "9884": {"comment":"Nothing to add?"},
        "9887": {"comment":"B = the figure"},
        "9888": {"synopsis":"Adds one to the message's two digits, B times.","comment":"Add one to the two digits"},
        "9896": {"synopsis":"Prints the figure and, at 3 % or more, the warning.","comment":"\"Spin speed difference\" with the figure"},
        "9901": {"comment":"3 % or more?"},
        "9904": {"comment":"Then \"Spin speed is INCORRECT !\""},
        "9910": {"comment":"Carry set if under 3 %"},
        "9911": {"comment":"A = $FF"},
        "9914": {"synopsis":"Adds one to the decimal number whose last ASCII digit is at HL, carrying into the digits\nbefore it.\nEntry: HL = the last digit.\nChanges: AF, HL.","comment":"Add one to the digit at HL"},
        "9917": {"comment":"Past '9'?"},
        "9920": {"comment":"Back to '0', carrying into the digit before"},
        "9925": {"synopsis":"Reads a sector of track D of the drive at $6AA4 into the buffer at $6861 through DOS_JUMPS\n$0163 (B = 0, E = 0, IX = $6A61) and checks that all 512 bytes equal the filler at $6860. B\nis set to 9 and E to B - 1, but no loop follows and E is then set to 0, so one sector a\ntrack is read.\nEntry: D = the track.\nExit: carry set if every byte matched; carry clear with A = $FF after \"Data not read\ncorrectly.\", or with A = the error DOS_JUMPS $0163 returned.","comment":"B = 9 (no loop follows)"},
        "9929": {"comment":"C = the drive"},
        "9932": {"comment":"E = B - 1, overwritten below"},
        "9934": {"comment":"B = 0"},
        "9936": {"comment":"E = 0"},
        "9938": {"comment":"HL = the sector buffer"},
        "9941": {"comment":"IX = the parameter block"},
        "9945": {"comment":"ROM 2 and RAM bank 7 in"},
        "9948": {"comment":"DOS_JUMPS $0163: the sector into the buffer"},
        "9951": {"comment":"ROM 1 and RAM bank 0 back in"},
        "9954": {"comment":"Failed?"},
        "9955": {"comment":"Failed?"},
        "9957": {"comment":"512 bytes from the buffer"},
        "9963": {"synopsis":"One byte of the buffer against the filler (DT_READ_CHECK).","comment":"Each the expected byte?"},
        "9969": {"comment":"Next byte"},
        "9971": {"comment":"All 512?"},
        "9975": {"comment":"Carry set: every byte matched"},
        "9978": {"synopsis":"A byte did not match: report it.","comment":"\"Data not read correctly.\""},
        "9984": {"comment":"Carry clear and A = $FF: already reported"},
        "9988": {"synopsis":"Formats track D of the drive at $6AA4 through DOS_JUMPS $016C, filled with the byte at\n$6860: E = the filler, B = 0, C = the drive, HL = the sector list built at $6A7B\n(DT_FORMAT_LIST), IX = $6A61.\nEntry: D = the track.\nExit: as DOS_JUMPS $016C returns (carry set on success, otherwise A = the error).","comment":"E = the filler byte"},
        "9992": {"comment":"B = 0"},
        "9994": {"comment":"C = the drive"},
        "9998": {"comment":"HL = the sector list for track D"},
        "10004": {"comment":"IX = the parameter block"},
        "10008": {"comment":"ROM 2 and RAM bank 7 in"},
        "10011": {"comment":"DOS_JUMPS $016C: format track D"},
        "10014": {"comment":"ROM 1 and RAM bank 0 back in"},
        "10018": {"synopsis":"Builds the list of sector IDs for formatting a track: nine entries of four bytes, track D,\nhead 0, sectors 1 to 9 and size code 2 (512 bytes).\nEntry: HL = the list, D = the track.\nChanges: nothing.","comment":"Keep AF, BC and HL"},
        "10021": {"comment":"Nine sectors"},
        "10023": {"synopsis":"One sector's ID (DT_FORMAT_LIST).","comment":"Track D"},
        "10025": {"comment":"Head 0"},
        "10028": {"comment":"Sector 1 to 9"},
        "10033": {"comment":"Size code 2: 512 bytes"},
        "10036": {"comment":"Next entry"},
        "10042": {"synopsis":"Waits until the drive is ready, calls DOS_JUMPS $0196 (which turns the motor on) and times\nDT_TIME_READ with interrupts off.\nExit: DE:HL = the count.","comment":"Wait until the drive is ready"},
        "10047": {"comment":"ROM 2 and RAM bank 7 in"},
        "10050": {"comment":"DOS_JUMPS $0196: the motor on"},
        "10053": {"comment":"ROM 1 and RAM bank 0 back in"},
        "10056": {"comment":"Time the command with interrupts off"},
        "10062": {"synopsis":"Waits until the controller is not busy, sends the 765's READ DATA ($66: MFM, skip deleted\ndata) for the drive at $6AA4, cylinder 0, head 0, sector $FE, size code 3, last sector $FE,\ngap $2A, data length $FF, then counts in DE:HL while the main status register (port $2FFD)\ndoes not show bit 7. A data byte in the execution phase (bit 5) is read from port $3FFD and\nthe count goes on; otherwise it waits for bit 7 and returns with the result bytes unread.\nExit: DE:HL = the count.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"Controller busy (bit 4)?"},
        "10071": {"comment":"The 765's READ DATA, MFM, skip deleted data"},
        "10076": {"comment":"The drive, head 0"},
        "10082": {"comment":"Cylinder 0"},
        "10086": {"comment":"Head 0"},
        "10090": {"comment":"Sector $FE"},
        "10095": {"comment":"Size code 3"},
        "10100": {"comment":"Last sector $FE"},
        "10105": {"comment":"Gap length $2A"},
        "10110": {"comment":"Data length $FF"},
        "10115": {"comment":"DE:HL = 0, the count"},
        "10121": {"synopsis":"Points BC at the main status register again and counts on.","comment":"Main status register"},
        "10124": {"synopsis":"Counts until the controller shows bit 7 (DT_TIME_READ)."},
        "10126": {"comment":"Ready for the processor (bit 7)?"},
        "10130": {"comment":"Count one more"},
        "10131": {"comment":"Low word wrapped?"},
        "10135": {"comment":"Carry into the high word"},
        "10138": {"synopsis":"Bit 7 set: a data byte, or the end of the command?","comment":"Execution phase (bit 5)?"},
        "10142": {"comment":"Take a data byte and count on"},
        "10149": {"synopsis":"Waits for bit 7 of the main status register.","comment":"Wait until the result phase is ready"},
        "10159": {"synopsis":"Sends A to the 765: waits until the main status register (port $2FFD) reads ready, direction\nto the controller, not in execution (bits 7-5 = 100), writes A to the data register (port\n$3FFD) and waits a little.\nEntry: A = the byte.\nChanges: AF, BC, D.","comment":"D = the byte to send"},
        "10160": {"comment":"Main status register"},
        "10163": {"synopsis":"Waits for the controller to take a byte."},
        "10165": {"comment":"Ready for a byte from the processor?"},
        "10171": {"comment":"Send it to the data register"},
        "10177": {"comment":"Short delay"},
        "10182": {"synopsis":"Reads the status of the drive at $6AA4 through DOS_JUMPS $017E, waits $4000 counts, reads it\nagain and keeps its bit 5 (ready).\nExit: A = the status AND $20; zero flag clear if the drive is ready.","comment":"C = the drive"},
        "10186": {"comment":"ROM 2 and RAM bank 7 in"},
        "10189": {"comment":"DOS_JUMPS $017E: the drive's status"},
        "10192": {"comment":"ROM 1 and RAM bank 0 back in"},
        "10195": {"comment":"Wait a while"},
        "10198": {"synopsis":"Counts BC down to 0.","comment":"Count down"},
        "10205": {"comment":"C = the drive"},
        "10209": {"comment":"The drive's status again"},
        "10212": {"comment":"DOS_JUMPS $017E again"},
        "10215": {"comment":"ROM 1 and RAM bank 0 back in"},
        "10218": {"comment":"Ready (bit 5)?"},
        "10221": {"synopsis":"Prints message A of the test's own messages (DT_MESSAGES) through DT_PRINT_NTH, with SCR_CT\nset to $FF so the screen scrolls without asking.\nEntry: A = the message number.","comment":"Keep the message number"},
        "10222": {"comment":"No \"scroll?\" prompts: SCR_CT = $FF"},
        "10228": {"comment":"HL = the test's messages"},
        "10231": {"comment":"Print message A"},
        "10234": {"synopsis":"The test's messages, $00 ending each, $0D for a new line: 0 an empty line, 1 \"Integral disk\ntest  V1.5\", 2 \"Found Drive(s) :A\", 3 \"NO DISK INTERFACE !\" and \"Test Aborted.\", 4 \"Testing\nDrive \", 5 \"Insert side 1 of test disk.\", 6 \"Remove disk from drive\", 7 \"Insert side 2 of\ntest disk.\", 8 \"Disk is not write-protected.\", 9 \"Spin test not implemented.\" (not used), 10\n\"Checking Data.\", 11 \"Starting spin-speed test.\", 12 \"Data not read correctly.\", 13 \"Press R\nto repeat, Q to quit\", 14 \"Formatting tracks.\", 15 \"Spin speed difference *00 %\"\n(DT_SPIN_TEST writes the sign at $297D and the digits at $297E), 16 \"Spin speed is INCORRECT\n!\", then the two verdicts that DT_START prints from their own addresses, \"The disk drive\ntest passed.\" ($29A0) and \"The disk drive test failed.\" ($29BD). In RAM the table is at\n$639E."},
        "10714": {"synopsis":"Prints AT 0,0, keeping AF. Nothing calls it.","comment":"Keep AF"},
        "10715": {"comment":"Print AT 0,0"},
        "10724": {"synopsis":"Prints the message for disk error A (DT_ERROR_TEXTS) and a new line. Errors 10 and over take\nentry A - 10.\nEntry: A = the error number.","comment":"HL = the disk error messages"},
        "10727": {"comment":"Error 10 or more?"},
        "10731": {"comment":"Those are entry A - 10"},
        "10733": {"synopsis":"Prints the entry.","comment":"Print the entry"},
        "10736": {"comment":"End the line"},
        "10740": {"synopsis":"Prints string A of a list of strings each ended by $00, up to its $00 or a $FF.\nEntry: A = the string's number (0 for the first), HL = the list.","comment":"B = A + 1 strings to pass"},
        "10742": {"comment":"A = 0, the terminator"},
        "10743": {"synopsis":"Passes one string (DT_PRINT_NTH).","comment":"DE = this string's start"},
        "10745": {"synopsis":"Looks for the string's $00.","comment":"At its terminator?"},
        "10749": {"comment":"Next string"},
        "10751": {"comment":"HL = string A's start"},
        "10752": {"synopsis":"Prints the string at HL up to a $00 or $FF, through ROM 3's $0010.\nEntry: HL = the string.\nExit: HL = the address after the terminator.","comment":"Next character"},
        "10754": {"comment":"Terminator $00?"},
        "10756": {"comment":"Or $FF?"},
        "10759": {"comment":"Print it (ROM 3's $0010)"},
        "10764": {"synopsis":"The disk error messages, $00 ending each, for DT_PRINT_ERROR: entries 0-9 \"Drive not\nready.\", \"Disc is write protected.\", \"Disc seek fail.\", \"Disc CRC data error.\", \"No data on\ndisc.\", \"Address mark missing.\", \"Unrecognized disc format.\", \"Unknown disc error. - Well\ndone !\", \"Disc changed while in use.\", \"Wrong type of disc in drive.\"; entries 10-27 (errors\n20-37) \"Bad filename.\", \"Bad parameter.\", \"Drive not found.\", \"File not found.\", \"File\nalready exists.\", \"End of file.\", \"Disc full.\", \"Directory full.\", \"Read-only file.\", \"File\nnot open, or wrong access.\", \"Access denied, file in use.\", \"Cannot rename between drives\",\n\"Extent is missing.\", \"Uncached. (software error)\", \"File too big.\", \"Disc not bootable\",\n\"Drive was in use.\", \"You should never see this.\". In RAM the table is at $65B0."},
        "11349": {"synopsis":"Waits for a key: clears bit 5 of FLAGS, waits until the interrupt sets it again, and takes\nLAST_K.\nExit: A = the key's code.\nChanges: AF, HL.","comment":"FLAGS bit 5: no new key yet"},
        "11354": {"synopsis":"Waits for FLAGS bit 5.","comment":"Wait for the interrupt to take a key"},
        "11358": {"comment":"A = LAST_K"},
        "11361": {"comment":"Taken"},
        "11364": {"synopsis":"Pages ROM 0 and RAM bank 0 in with interrupts off and jumps to $0000. Nothing calls it.","comment":"Interrupts off for good"},
        "11365": {"comment":"Port $1FFD = 0"},
        "11371": {"comment":"Port $7FFD = 0: ROM 0 and RAM bank 0"},
        "11376": {"comment":"Restart the machine"},
        "11379": {"synopsis":"Pages this ROM (ROM 2) and RAM bank 7 in, keeping the copies at $5B5C and $5B67 up to date,\nso that the test can call DOS_JUMPS.\nChanges: nothing.","comment":"Interrupts off while paging"},
        "11380": {"comment":"Keep AF, BC and HL"},
        "11383": {"comment":"Port $7FFD and its copy at $5B5C"},
        "11389": {"comment":"RAM bank 7 at $C000, ROM bit 0 clear"},
        "11395": {"comment":"Page it"},
        "11397": {"comment":"$5B67: ROM bit 1 set, so ROM 2"},
        "11404": {"comment":"Port $1FFD"},
        "11409": {"comment":"Restore HL, BC and AF"},
        "11414": {"synopsis":"Pages ROM 1 and RAM bank 0 back in, keeping the copies at $5B5C and $5B67 up to date.\nChanges: nothing.","comment":"Interrupts off while paging"},
        "11415": {"comment":"Keep AF, BC and HL"},
        "11418": {"comment":"Port $7FFD and its copy at $5B5C"},
        "11424": {"comment":"RAM bank 0 at $C000, ROM bit 0 set"},
        "11430": {"comment":"Page it"},
        "11432": {"comment":"$5B67: ROM bit 1 clear, so ROM 1"},
        "11440": {"comment":"Port $1FFD"},
        "11445": {"comment":"Restore HL, BC and AF"},
        "11450": {"synopsis":"Three bytes after the last routine: $00, $00, $E5. They are copied with the program and are\nthe first values of its variables at $685E (the word DT_SPIN_TEST keeps a count in) and\n$6860 (the filler byte, so the first DT_FORMAT_TRACK of a run fills track 0 with $E5)."},
        "11453": {"synopsis":"Unused: $00 up to $2CDF; FILL_2CE0 goes on to $3DFF. ROM 0 copies the part up to $305B with\nthe program, where the sector buffer ($6861) and the parameter block ($6A61) lie."},
        "16383": {"synopsis":"The last byte, $66."}
      }
    }
  },
